        "original_id": "e048d5e9-65b1-593a-a25a-1016dd881d3a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Deal, Kent, England, Greenwich, UK\n- Structures: Deal Timeball, waterfront four-storey tower\n- Systems: Greenwich Mean Time, UTC, UT1\n- Topics: navigation, UK civil timekeeping, mean solar time\n\nFacts:\n- Deal Timeball is a Victorian maritime Greenwich Mean Time signal located on the roof of a waterfront four-storey tower in Deal, Kent, England.\n- Today, Greenwich Mean Time is considered equivalent to UTC for UK civil purposes, although this equivalence is not formalised.\n- For navigation, Greenwich Mean Time is considered equivalent to UT1, which is the modern form of mean solar time at 0° longitude.\n- UTC and UT1 can differ by up to 0.9 seconds, so the term Greenwich Mean Time should not be used for precise purposes.",
